   336	    """
   337	    Expand a separated 3x3 block motif into a separator-filled 5x5 lattice.
   338	
   339	    Input structure:
   340	    - One motif sits on a uniform background, and the motif is 11x11 rather than 9x9.
   341	    - It consists of nine logical 3x3 slots arranged in a 3x3 array, with 1-pixel
   342	      separator rows and columns between neighboring slots.
   343	    - Eight slots contain colored 3x3 blocks, the middle slot is background, and
   344	      the separator color outlines the missing center.
   345	
   346	    Rule:
   347	    - Detect the separator color and parse the visible pattern as 3x3 blocks on a
   348	      pitch of four pixels.
   349	    - Reconstruct the missing center block from the eight inward-facing pixels
   350	      around the hole, using the majority non-separator color for the center cell.
   351	    - Copy each visible block to its point-symmetric outer slot in the implied 5x5
   352	      layout, keep the separator lattice continuous, and fill the otherwise empty
   353	      3x3 logical slots with the separator color instead of background.
   354	
   355	    Key insight:
   356	    - The separator is structural twice over: first it reveals how to parse the
   357	      input into blocks plus gutters, and then it acts as the material that fills
   358	      the unused expanded slots. Solving the task requires extending the whole
   359	      separator framework, not just copying blocks.
